{# Photo gallery for a taxon page. Shared by species-detail.njk and genus.njk.

   Lifted out of species-detail.njk (beeatlas-xrg): 39 genus entries carried 119
   photos that no template rendered, so every one of them — including the five
   curator-accepted Diadasia photos — was seeded, validated and shown to nobody.

   `entry` is a photos[...] value; `label` is the taxon name, used as the alt-text
   fallback when a photo has no caption. Callers look the entry up themselves
   because the key differs by rank (sp.scientificName vs genus.genus).

   The empty-entry branch renders the "No photo available" placeholder, which is
   the species page's established behaviour: it holds one cell of a grid whose
   other cell is a full stat row. genus.njk deliberately does NOT call the macro
   when it has no photos — see the comment there.

   NOT wired to subgenus.njk, tribe.njk or subfamily.njk, deliberately. Tribe and
   subfamily have no path to a manifest entry: the seeder pages over species.json,
   which holds species and genera only. Subgenus is worse than merely empty — a
   nominate subgenus shares its genus's name (Stelis (Stelis), Apis (Apis),
   Triepeolus (Triepeolus) are 3 of the 111 built subgenus pages), so a lookup by
   bare name would silently show the GENUS's photos on a subgenus page and
   attribute a broader taxon's images to a narrower one. Wiring subgenus needs a
   rank-qualified key first. #}

{% macro gallery(entry, label) %}
{# One <figure> per photo, baked. bee-photo-gallery reads these and upgrades
   them into a strip + lightbox; without JS they stand as a plain stack, each
   with its own attribution (which is per-photo, not per-species). #}
{%- if entry and entry.photos and entry.photos.length > 0 -%}
<bee-photo-gallery class="photo-gallery">
  {%- for p in entry.photos -%}
  <figure class="hero-photo">
    <img
      class="photo-hero"
      src="{{ p.src or p.url }}"
      {% if p.srcset %}srcset="{{ p.srcset }}" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw"{% endif %}
      {% if p.square %}data-square="{{ p.square }}"{% endif %}
      {% if p.large %}data-large="{{ p.large }}"{% endif %}
      {% if p.attribution %}data-attribution="{{ p.attribution }}"{% endif %}
      {% if p.observation_id %}data-observation-url="https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/{{ p.observation_id }}"{% endif %}
      {# The first photo is the LCP candidate — eager, and flagged so the
         intent is explicit rather than an absent attribute. The rest defer. #}
      {% if loop.first %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}
      alt="{{ p.caption or label }}">
    {%- if p.attribution -%}
    <figcaption class="attribution">{{ p.attribution }}</figcaption>
    {%- endif -%}
  </figure>
  {%- endfor -%}
</bee-photo-gallery>
{%- else -%}
<figure class="hero-photo">
  <div class="photo-placeholder">No photo available</div>
</figure>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}
